{
  "email": "leo.martins@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify sender, department/title and laptop for software request"
}

{
  "query": "Zoom Company Portal",
  "reason": "Check whether Zoom is an approved Company Portal app"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, happy to help you get ready for tomorrow's client meeting. Here's the quickest way: 1) Open the Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop and search for \"Zoom\". If it's there, click Install. You don't need IT for that and it only takes a few minutes. 2) If Zoom isn't listed, installing it needs your manager's approval and a security review. Please reply to this ticket with your manager's name and have them reply to say they approve. Once we have that, we'll pass it on to get it installed. Please don't install Zoom from a download link or a link someone emailed you. For tomorrow, you can usually join a Zoom meeting from your web browser without installing anything. Open the client's invite link and choose \"Join from your browser\". Let us know what you find in the Company Portal.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is Leo Martins (user_id 6), Account Executive in Sales, laptop BL-LT-0106. The account is active with no problems. He's asking for the Zoom client for a client meeting tomorrow. Following KB-027: I have no tool to check the Company Portal catalog, so I sent the user there first. If Zoom isn't in the portal, we need manager approval plus a security review. Then escalate to Tier 2 with the app name (Zoom Workplace client, latest version), the business reason (external client meetings in Sales), and who approved it. I suggested the Zoom browser join option for tomorrow. No admin rights or credentials were given. No escalation yet because there's no approval on file.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
